{"id": "EUVD-2026-97359", "enisaUuid": "994f91de-eced-3d0b-971a-72db611722ac", "description": "RT-Thread through 5.3.0 contains a memory corruption vulnerability in the legacy USB CDC virtual COM port driver that aliases rx_ringbuffer as a Serial V2 rt_serial_rx_fifo in _function_enable(). A connected USB host configuring the CDC device triggers writes past the ring buffer into struct vcom members and an invalid rt_free() on close, causing denial of service.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T12:13:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T14:59:23", "baseScore": 5.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:P/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/RT-Thread/rt-thread/issues/11739", "https://github.com/RT-Thread/rt-thread/pull/11770", "https://github.com/RT-Thread/rt-thread/commit/ceef6e0ccd646aef61b907aeb9f29269d1caba50", "https://github.com/RT-Thread/rt-thread/blob/99428a1e7f7447955aa860f7c969273a12095b8f/components/legacy/usb/usbdevice/class/cdc_vcom.c#L518", "https://github.com/RT-Thread/rt-thread", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/rt-thread-through-5.3.0-memory-corruption-via-usb-cdc-vcom-driver"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108952", "GHSA-x4hq-c3c6-m368"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "770edcd1-2299-393d-8599-7f6f7f244a43", "product": {"name": "RT-Thread", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22645.3.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ecf271eb-9cdc-3c3c-9d86-7b9dff2146e7", "vendor": {"name": "RT-Thread"}}], "isExploited": false}